// Time-based rate limit (token bucket). Unlike rate_limit.pfc, which caps the
// cumulative number of segments on a connection, `rate(per_second, burst)` is a
// real rate: a bucket of `burst` tokens that refills at `per_second` tokens/sec.
// Each packet spends one token; `rate(...)` is true when the bucket is empty
// (the flow is over its allowed rate), so this drops the excess and lets the
// flow resume as the bucket refills. State (tokens + last-refill time) lives in
// the flow, keyed on the connection.
//
// Here: allow bursts of up to 20 requests, then a steady 5 requests/sec per
// connection on :80; drop anything faster.
filter {
  if (proto != 6) return pass;          // TCP
  if (dport != 80) return pass;
  if (len == 0) return pass;            // don't spend tokens on pure ACKs
  if (rate(5, 20)) {
    log(2);                             // over the limit -> tell userspace
    return drop("too_fast");
  }
  return pass;
}
